# Archcheck binary (built locally by scripts/archcheck/).
# Anchored with leading '/' so the pattern matches only the root-level
# build artifact. Without the anchor, gitignore treats `archcheck` as
# matching any PATH COMPONENT named that way, which recursively excludes
# the entire `scripts/archcheck/` tree (the W1 PR1 regression surfaced this).
/archcheck

# Qdrant reindex binary (built locally from cmd/admin/reindex_qdrant*.go).
# Anchored with leading '/' so the pattern matches only the root-level
# build artifact. Without the anchor, gitignore would match any PATH
# COMPONENT named that way, which could recursively exclude future source
# trees with the same path component. 58.8MB ELF executable (dynamically
# linked, includes debug info); not a test fixture (zero Go/MD/sh/py/yaml
# references repo-wide — same forward-prevention pattern as /archcheck).
/_reindex_qdrant

# Seed test asset binary (built locally from cmd/admin/seed_test_asset/*.go).
# Anchored with leading '/' so the pattern matches only the root-level
# build artifact. 8.8MB ELF executable (dynamically linked, includes debug
# info). The 2 source-file 'seed_test_asset' mentions in tracked code
# (tests/e2e/qdrant_dod_4_assertions_test.go + cmd/admin/qdrant_preflight_stubs.go)
# are doc comments referring to the Go SOURCE path cmd/admin/seed_test_asset/seed.go,
# not invocations of this root binary — same forward-prevention pattern as
# /_reindex_qdrant. Rebuild on demand: `go build -o seed_test_asset ./cmd/admin/seed_test_asset/`.
/seed_test_asset

# Worker integration reference binary (built locally from tests/operational/worker-integration/main.go).
# Anchored with leading '/' so the pattern matches only the root-level build artifact
# (NOT recursive source-file exclusion under tests/operational/worker-integration/). 9.16 MB ELF
# (dynamically linked, includes debug info). Forward-prevention per godlike/07 — same
# pattern as /archcheck + /_reindex_qdrant + /seed_test_asset. Rebuild on demand:
#   go build -o worker_integration ./tests/operational/worker-integration/main.go
/worker_integration

# Docker secrets (never commit tokens)
secrets/

# Whisper worker Python venv (faster-whisper + CTranslate2 + CUDA 12 wheels).
# Host-side venv used by `make whisper-preflight` and the systemd
# ExecStartPre gate. Recreate it on demand with the curated lockfile:
#   python3 -m venv .venv-whisper
#   .venv-whisper/bin/python -m pip install --no-cache-dir \
#       -r requirements/whisper.lock.txt
# Then verify with: make whisper-preflight [VELOX_WHISPER_DEVICE=cuda]
.venv-whisper/

# Argos host-side Python venv (argos pipeline tooling).
.venv-argos/

# PR1 (Repository truth, June 2026):
#   * scripts/archcheck/current_report.json is a per-run diagnostic snapshot
#     of the codebase scan; regenerated cheaply on every `go run ./scripts/archcheck`.
#   * It is NEVER used as an allowlist (see docs/migrations/api-infrastructure-imports-allowlist.txt
#     for the single source of truth on the ratchet).
#   * Keeping it out-of-tree avoids polluting PR diffs with full-repo snapshots.
scripts/archcheck/current_report.json
# Validation transient logs (NOT shipped):
ci_output.txt
ci_full_output.txt
/tmp/build.out
/tmp/vet.out
/tmp/test.out

# ci/archcheck-hard-fail: E2E sentinel marker for scripts/ci-archcheck-e2e.sh.
# The file is created + deleted by the E2E harness; if a run aborts
# mid-step (SIGINT, OOM, runner network drop) the sentinel is left
# orphaned on disk. gitignore it so subsequent CI + local pre-commit
# runs do not see it as an unintended violation.
internal/api/_dummy_archcheck_regression.go

# Wave staging artefacts: temp splice blocks + python runners used by an
# operator-only pipeline (e.g. `.wave23_piper.py`) to register a wave
# entry on origin/main. The artefacts are single-use per wave and SHOULD
# NOT be committed — `.wave23_*` glob catches the canonical pre-commit
# state. Was leak-prone in June 2026 when these landed in the working
# tree between the fast-forward and the conditional cleanup; this entry
# closes the gap (housekeeping precondition for the next wave).
.wave23_*
# Scratch quarantine - never-tracked prior in-progress work (P0.4 / P0.3 voiceover scratch)
# Moved 2026-06-29 as part of P0.6 closure so canonical main stays build-clean.
docs/notes/scratch/

# PR-A (June 2026): anti-reintro gate for diagnostic / snapshot artefacts
# that historically leaked into the working tree during mega-batch
# commits (the paste audit `tmp-diag` family). Patterns are
# subdir-safe via the trailing `/` (anchored to root) and case-sensitive
# (matches the rg-dir basename, NOT a substring of a longer name like
# `make-tmp-diag.sh`). CI enforcement lives in
# scripts/ci-architectural-checks.sh::Check 36 (forward-prevention gate,
# mirrors Check 5 / Check 8 alignment).
.tmp-diag/
tmp-diag/
CURRENT_*.go
TODO[0-9]*.go

# TTS-cleaned voiceover artifacts (regenerated from lyrics pipeline)
/cleaned_*.mp3
/cleaned_*.wav
/cleaned_*.ogg

# ============================================
# Root-level voiceover test artifacts (Phase 0 carry-forward, 2026-07-04)
# ============================================
# 7 untracked MP3 files appeared at repo root after manual voiceover
# test runs during Phase 0 of the operator test battery (filename
# patterns: prima-frase-*, questo-*, smoke-test-*, test-*, verifica-*).
# Anchor with leading '/' so the pattern matches only root-level
# artifacts (NOT legitimate .mp3 fixtures anywhere else in the tree).
# Mirrors the anchored-binary pattern of /pipelinegen + /server +
# /worker. Forward-pointer: PR-PHASE-0-VOICEOVER-CLEANUP if user later
# wants to whitelist specific MP3 fixtures.
/*.mp3
/*.wav
/*.ogg

# ============================================
# Voiceover test artifacts - user-spec defense-in-depth (2026-07-04)
# ============================================
# User-spec 2026-07-04: 6 patterns added per explicit user instruction.
# The 5 anchored root-level patterns (below) ARE redundant with the existing
# /*.mp3 canonical pattern; the unanchored *.mp3 is the only NEW pattern
# (catches any .mp3 file anywhere in the tree - regression risk on legitimate
# test subdir fixtures was explicitly accepted by the user per godlike/07
# no-fake-availability disclosure in this commit body).
*.mp3
/prima-frase-*.mp3
/smoke-test-voiceover-pipeline*.mp3
/test-*.mp3
/verifica-postfix-*.mp3
/questo-*.mp3

# ============================================
# Voiceover fixture negation patterns (cfa088cf follow-up, 2026-07-04)
# ============================================
# Defense-in-depth against the unanchored `*.mp3` pattern (added in
# cfa088cf). The unanchored pattern catches ANY .mp3 file in the tree;
# if a legitimate voiceover/audio test fixture ships at tests/fixtures/
# or internal/**/testdata/, it would be silently ignored without these
# negations. The two negation patterns preserve legitimate fixtures
# without restoring untracked root-level test output (the latter still
# receives defensive coverage via /*.mp3 + /prima-frase-*.mp3 etc.).
!tests/fixtures/**/*.mp3

# Allow canonical-path media fixtures (mirror the .mp3 pattern above) +
# prevent repo-root pollution per AGENTS.md #8 housekeeping rules:
# per godlike/07 honest scope-lock, binary media fixtures (e.g.
# test_*.mp4, sample_*.mp4) MUST live at tests/fixtures/<domain>/,
# NEVER at the repo root.
/test_*.mp4
/sample_*.mp4
/*.mp4
!tests/fixtures/**/*.mp4
!internal/**/testdata/**/*.mp3

